Finding from k5 (sick-worker, 2026-10-10). SICK::Issuer::StepCA root_pem does not check that ca.root is self-signed and a CA. Pointed at the intermediate, step still works (Go trusts any certificate in the pool as an anchor), SICK judges devices against the intermediate, and sick trust hands the intermediate to clients as their root - everything breaks at the next intermediate rotation. Done when: loading a non-self-signed or non-CA root is an error naming ca.root and the reason (SICK::Bundle::is_self_signed exists), with a test.

sick-worker: started. Plan: checks in StepCA root_pem/intermediates_pem (runner already calls both inside the per-device eval), two additive SICK::Bundle methods is_ca and signs_itself; messages renamed from 'CA root'/'CA intermediates' to 'ca.root'/'ca.intermediates'.

